---
title: FortiGate Admin Activity via jsconsole (CVE-2024-55591)
id: 443cd001-5181-4eaf-8f29-bb30a118534b
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects FortiOS administrator logins and new admin account creation performed
    through the jsconsole management interface, the pattern Fortinet published as an
    indicator of CVE-2024-55591 exploitation. The Gentlemen use this flaw as their
    primary initial access vector.
references:
    - https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-24-535
    - https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-55591
    - https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/threat-actor/6387/the-gentlemen-ransomware
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026-08-23
modified: 2026-11-03
tags:
    - attack.initial-access
    - attack.t1190
    - attack.persistence
    - attack.t1136.001
    - cve.2024-55591
logsource:
    product: fortios
    service: event
detection:
    selection_ui:
        ui|contains: 'jsconsole'
    selection_login:
        logdesc: 'Admin login successful'
    selection_admin_add:
        logdesc: 'Object attribute configured'
        cfgpath: 'system.admin'
        action: 'Add'
    condition: selection_ui and (selection_login or selection_admin_add)
falsepositives:
    - Administrators who legitimately use the jsconsole CLI widget in the GUI; baseline expected admin accounts and source IPs
level: high

